---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import SectionHeader from "../components/SectionHeader.astro";

const hasPhoto = true;
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About | Syntheion Dynamics"
  description="Daniel — neurodivergent maker, sci-fi worldbuilder, and indie dev working toward a 2027 sabbatical."
  mode="archive"
  sector="About"
  ogImage="/images/mini-astrum-landscape.jpg"
>
  <section class="section container">
    <SectionHeader sector="Profile" title="Daniel" subtitle="Maker. Worldbuilder. Game director in progress." />

    <div class={hasPhoto ? "bio-grid" : ""}>
      <div class="bio-text">
        <p>
          I am 29, neurodivergent (ADHD and autism), and I live independently in a small house near Jeseník nad Odrou.
          I work a day job as a maintenance coordinator. That funds everything else.
        </p>
        <p>
          I studied electronic computer systems, but I do not think of myself as a technician. My actual operating mode
          is closer to creative director — I define the vision and the architecture, AI helps me implement. I build
          things that did not exist before and that I personally needed to exist.
        </p>
        <p>
          The plan is a sabbatical in May 2027. Finish the Astrum Invictum playable demo, launch a Kickstarter, and
          exit wage work into full independent development. That is the timeline I am working against.
        </p>
        <p>
          I use AI as a genuine creative partner and cognitive scaffolding, not as a shortcut. That distinction matters
          to me.
        </p>
      </div>

      {hasPhoto && (
        <div class="photo-slot">
          <img src="/images/mini-about-daniel.jpg" alt="Daniel" class="profile-photo enlargeable" />
        </div>
      )}
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section container">
    <SectionHeader sector="Projects" title="What I am building" />
    <div class="grid-2">
      <div class="panel">
        <p class="eyebrow">[ACTIVE]</p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Astrum Invictum</strong> — transmedia sci-fi, Unity HDRP demo, 10+ months of development</li>
          <li><strong>Bungač Engine</strong> — custom C# engine that became an immersive sim horror project</li>
          <li><strong>Gooblerator</strong> — VST3 guitar amp sim, release-ready</li>
          <li><strong>ADHD Planner</strong> — node canvas I built because nothing else fit my brain</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="panel">
        <p class="eyebrow">[BACKGROUND TRACKS]</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Organic plant growing with a DIY low-watt system (ROOTFRAME + LOT technique)</li>
          <li>Hiking around Jeseník nad Odrou</li>
          <li>Private hardware tinkering</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="muted" style="margin-top: 0.8rem;">
          Building output since 2024: 2 VST plugins, 1 planning tool, 1 game engine, 1 transmedia project.
          All solo, most of it in evenings and weekends.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section container">
    <SectionHeader sector="References" title="What shaped the aesthetic" />
    <div class="grid-2">
      <div class="panel">
        <p class="eyebrow">[SCI-FI WITH SOUL]</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Star Trek DS9 — ethics under pressure, institutional weight</li>
          <li>Red Dwarf — loneliness and absurdity at the edge of known space</li>
          <li>Outer Wilds — presence, curiosity, and the physics of grief</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="panel">
        <p class="eyebrow">[GAMES THAT LEFT SOMETHING BEHIND]</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Deus Ex: Human Revolution</li>
          <li>System Shock (remake)</li>
          <li>Colony Ship</li>
          <li>Mass Effect</li>
          <li>Cyberpunk 2077</li>
          <li>The Witcher 3</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section container">
    <SectionHeader sector="Interests" title="What I think about when I am not building" />
    <div class="panel">
      <p>
        Relativity, black holes, and the hard edges of astrophysics. Ontology and the question of what it means for
        anything to exist at all. Why some games feel like they hand you something real and others just consume time.
        Whether consciousness is substrate-independent. Why DS9 holds up better than most modern prestige television.
      </p>
      <p class="muted">
        I treat these not as casual interests but as the actual inputs to everything I create.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section container">
    <SectionHeader sector="Roadmap" title="2027 exit strategy" />
    <div class="panel">
      <p>
        May 2027: sabbatical begins. The objective is a playable Astrum Invictum demo ready for a Kickstarter campaign
        with a $10k goal — enough to fund 18 months of full-time independent development. After the car loan clears
        in May 2027, monthly expenses drop to around 8–9k CZK. The math works, if the demo is good enough.
      </p>
      <p class="muted">That is the bet. Everything else is preparation for it.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section container">
    <SectionHeader sector="Contact" title="Links" />
    <p>
      <a class="button" href="https://astruminvictum.com" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">astruminvictum.com</a>
    </p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .bio-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 280px;
    gap: 2rem;
    align-items: start;
  }

  .profile-photo {
    width: 100%;
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    filter: grayscale(20%);
  }

  @media (max-width: 900px) {
    .bio-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
  }
</style>
